1
00:00:04,504 --> 00:00:05,797
You bastard!

2
00:00:18,143 --> 00:00:20,020
I'll kill them all at once.

3
00:00:34,492 --> 00:00:36,161
Everyone, we're leaving the village.

4
00:00:39,748 --> 00:00:41,791
Sanada!

5
00:00:46,546 --> 00:00:48,214
Feel the weight of the lives…

6
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:51,885
you've taken!

7
00:01:10,278 --> 00:01:12,530
Her Ladyship, Lady Yodo.

8
00:01:17,285 --> 00:01:18,787
Raise your heads.

9
00:01:40,058 --> 00:01:41,142
Nobushige…

10
00:01:41,643 --> 00:01:43,144
LADY YODO

11
00:01:43,228 --> 00:01:45,230
You're the only one I can count on.

12
00:01:53,905 --> 00:01:55,490
What's Osaka like?

13
00:01:56,074 --> 00:01:59,494
I hear you can get a delicious
Western food called tempura there.

14
00:01:59,577 --> 00:02:00,745
Is that true?

15
00:02:00,829 --> 00:02:02,080
Tempura?

16
00:02:02,956 --> 00:02:04,499
You keep yapping about that.

17
00:02:04,582 --> 00:02:06,209
What can you expect?

18
00:02:06,292 --> 00:02:08,211
He has never left the village before.

19
00:02:08,795 --> 00:02:09,796
I see…

20
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:13,591
The Miyoshi brothers
are from Osaka, right?

21
00:02:13,675 --> 00:02:17,387
Yes. It was a lively, wonderful city.
Back in the Toyotomi days.

22
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:20,014
Seikai ran an apothecary there.

23
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:22,517
I hope you can do it again.

24
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:23,434
I hope so.

25
00:02:23,977 --> 00:02:26,521
Then you should open a restaurant too.

26
00:02:27,522 --> 00:02:28,439
That sounds good!

27
00:02:28,523 --> 00:02:30,275
You just want free food.

28
00:02:30,942 --> 00:02:32,277
All right, everyone!

29
00:02:36,447 --> 00:02:39,492
At this rate,
we'll reach Osaka Castle by tomorrow.

30
00:02:39,576 --> 00:02:43,830
That Tsuge ninja
is looking for us, isn't he?

31
00:02:45,206 --> 00:02:47,333
If we keep heading north,

32
00:02:47,417 --> 00:02:51,129
there's only one bridge across the river.

33
00:02:51,671 --> 00:02:55,258
Once we've crossed, we can destroy
the bridge and buy ourselves some time.

34
00:02:56,426 --> 00:02:57,260
Right.

35
00:02:59,304 --> 00:03:00,305
Are we on the right road?

36
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:02,390
Let me see.

37
00:03:02,891 --> 00:03:04,976
Hey, aren't those two a little too close?

38
00:03:05,768 --> 00:03:08,605
Kirigakure Saizo and Yuri Kamanosuke.

39
00:03:08,688 --> 00:03:11,316
They've been together
since they were kids.

40
00:03:11,983 --> 00:03:15,194
There's no room for you
to get between them.

41
00:03:15,945 --> 00:03:17,447
Let's take a break.

42
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:19,115
-Yes, let's take a break here.
-Yes.

43
00:03:19,198 --> 00:03:22,160
Hey, Yuri. Why do you go by Kamanosuke?

44
00:03:24,287 --> 00:03:25,622
None of your business.

45
00:03:25,705 --> 00:03:27,206
I wasn't asking you.

46
00:03:28,458 --> 00:03:30,376
North's that way.
We're on the right track.

47
00:03:31,294 --> 00:03:34,672
Come to think of it,
I never heard you thank me.

48
00:03:34,756 --> 00:03:35,673
What?

49
00:03:35,757 --> 00:03:38,051
You got out of the village thanks to me.

50
00:03:38,134 --> 00:03:39,969
All you did was climb a tree, monkey.

51
00:03:40,053 --> 00:03:41,596
What'd you say?

52
00:03:41,679 --> 00:03:42,513
No, no…

53
00:03:42,597 --> 00:03:46,017
We got out of the village thanks to Kakei.

54
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:47,143
I'm grateful.

55
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:48,061
KAKEI JUZO

56
00:03:48,144 --> 00:03:50,605
Even with 100 arrows,
you'd miss, Mochizuki.

57
00:03:51,731 --> 00:03:53,358
And he's coming with us too.

58
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:57,362
Ieyasu has killed many of my comrades.

59
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:02,367
I'll do what I can

60
00:04:03,326 --> 00:04:05,161
to honor them.

61
00:04:10,041 --> 00:04:11,709
Leave the support to me.

62
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:13,378
Much appreciated!

63
00:04:13,461 --> 00:04:16,673
Hey! I'm the one who brought Kakei along.

64
00:04:16,756 --> 00:04:20,551
That makes me the best of the bunch.
Right, old man Yukimura?

65
00:04:20,635 --> 00:04:21,678
That's right.

66
00:04:21,761 --> 00:04:22,762
Don't encourage him.

67
00:04:22,845 --> 00:04:24,514
He'll only get cockier.

68
00:04:24,597 --> 00:04:27,100
Wait, what did you even do?

69
00:04:27,183 --> 00:04:29,435
Shut up if you did nothing.

70
00:04:30,353 --> 00:04:31,187
What?

71
00:04:31,271 --> 00:04:32,230
"What?"

72
00:04:32,313 --> 00:04:34,065
You stand before our lord!

73
00:04:34,148 --> 00:04:35,984
Enough, you two!

74
00:04:45,910 --> 00:04:47,120
There's something we have

75
00:04:48,246 --> 00:04:49,622
that the Tokugawa don't.

76
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:52,208
Our bonds.

77
00:04:53,459 --> 00:04:54,627
To Ieyasu,

78
00:04:55,712 --> 00:04:58,172
his retainers
are nothing but disposable tools.

79
00:05:02,593 --> 00:05:03,511
And that…

80
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:05,263
is precisely

81
00:05:05,972 --> 00:05:07,307
their weakness.

82
00:05:09,058 --> 00:05:10,727
Our bonds, huh…

83
00:05:11,477 --> 00:05:13,396
Bound together, we can never be severed.

84
00:05:14,230 --> 00:05:15,315
Just like this cord.

85
00:05:32,123 --> 00:05:35,543
Well, I'm amazing even on my own.

86
00:05:39,505 --> 00:05:40,381
Shit…

87
00:05:43,551 --> 00:05:44,594
You frustrated?

88
00:05:46,387 --> 00:05:47,221
Shit.

89
00:05:48,347 --> 00:05:49,265
You're stepping on it.

90
00:05:52,268 --> 00:05:53,519
Gross!

91
00:05:53,603 --> 00:05:55,188
It's deer droppings!

92
00:05:55,813 --> 00:05:57,690
Kakei! Look!

93
00:05:57,774 --> 00:06:00,068
Yukimura has left Kudoyama?

94
00:06:00,151 --> 00:06:00,985
Yes, my lord.

95
00:06:01,069 --> 00:06:02,528
What a disgrace!

96
00:06:03,029 --> 00:06:04,072
You fool!

97
00:06:04,781 --> 00:06:07,116
You fool! Raise your head!

98
00:06:13,039 --> 00:06:13,998
Seize him.

99
00:06:16,918 --> 00:06:20,838
Under no circumstances can we let
Yukimura enter Osaka Castle.

100
00:06:27,053 --> 00:06:28,846
Where is the ninja?

101
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:29,764
Speak!

102
00:06:30,389 --> 00:06:31,349
Speak!

103
00:06:35,228 --> 00:06:36,604
A villager claims

104
00:06:37,605 --> 00:06:39,190
one of the ninja

105
00:06:40,108 --> 00:06:42,902
flew up to that watchtower.

106
00:06:42,985 --> 00:06:44,987
It was likely Sasuke.

107
00:06:46,072 --> 00:06:47,073
Sasuke?

108
00:06:48,116 --> 00:06:49,909
What shall we do with the villagers?

109
00:06:51,119 --> 00:06:52,745
Burn the entire village to the ground.

110
00:06:54,122 --> 00:06:56,499
It's Ogosho's order.

111
00:06:58,334 --> 00:06:59,168
Yes, my lord.

112
00:07:08,845 --> 00:07:09,679
What?

113
00:07:10,471 --> 00:07:11,431
What's wrong?

114
00:07:13,391 --> 00:07:14,767
The bridge is gone.

115
00:07:15,726 --> 00:07:17,395
It should be right here!

116
00:07:18,187 --> 00:07:20,690
The heavy rains last month
must've washed it away.

117
00:07:22,692 --> 00:07:24,777
So, what do we do now?

118
00:07:24,861 --> 00:07:26,028
Is there another way across?

119
00:07:26,612 --> 00:07:27,822
No.

120
00:07:27,905 --> 00:07:30,199
We'll have to backtrack
and find another route.

121
00:07:30,283 --> 00:07:33,035
We have to go all the way back?

122
00:07:34,537 --> 00:07:35,580
That's right!

123
00:07:37,290 --> 00:07:39,417
I came prepared for just such an occasion.

124
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:42,920
If we tie this to the opposite bank,
we should be able to cross.

125
00:07:43,629 --> 00:07:46,841
Not bad.
That's Sanada's strategist for you.

126
00:07:46,924 --> 00:07:48,301
How long is it?

127
00:07:48,384 --> 00:07:50,553
Well… 25 ken.

128
00:07:52,597 --> 00:07:54,557
It's 30 ken to the other bank.

129
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:56,058
So it's useless.

130
00:07:56,684 --> 00:07:57,727
I take it back.

131
00:08:01,606 --> 00:08:03,024
Okuni gave this to me.

132
00:08:04,358 --> 00:08:06,861
Here. I wove this with all my heart.

133
00:08:06,944 --> 00:08:08,946
I'm sure it'll protect you, Sasuke.

134
00:08:12,325 --> 00:08:16,120
Even with the knots, it's 35 ken long.
This will work.

135
00:08:16,204 --> 00:08:17,580
-Great.
-I take it back!

136
00:08:17,663 --> 00:08:18,915
Look at you, Master Strategist!

137
00:08:20,666 --> 00:08:21,834
What's wrong, Seikai?

138
00:08:22,793 --> 00:08:24,128
We can't cross this river.

139
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:29,008
Brother's afraid of water.
He nearly drowned when he was little.

140
00:08:30,968 --> 00:08:32,053
Sorry…

141
00:08:32,845 --> 00:08:33,971
I can't do this.

142
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:37,600
He's the worst.

143
00:08:37,683 --> 00:08:40,436
I mean, how are we even supposed to
get the rope to the other bank?

144
00:08:42,939 --> 00:08:44,106
Well…

145
00:08:45,233 --> 00:08:46,734
I take it back.

146
00:08:47,485 --> 00:08:48,819
What shall we do, my lord?

147
00:08:50,863 --> 00:08:51,697
We'll take a detour.

148
00:08:51,781 --> 00:08:53,282
What?!

149
00:08:56,619 --> 00:08:58,079
You…

150
00:08:59,330 --> 00:09:00,998
Let's just eat first.

151
00:09:01,832 --> 00:09:04,001
An army marches on its stomach.

152
00:09:04,085 --> 00:09:06,170
Like we have any food!

153
00:09:06,879 --> 00:09:07,713
Hey.

154
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:09,465
We do.

155
00:09:10,341 --> 00:09:12,301
You're the best!

156
00:09:13,177 --> 00:09:14,387
This place is dangerous.

157
00:09:14,470 --> 00:09:17,640
There's an abandoned village to the east
where we can hide.

158
00:09:17,723 --> 00:09:18,891
This is good.

159
00:09:21,477 --> 00:09:22,603
Something's coming.

160
00:09:23,813 --> 00:09:26,148
Lord Yukimura! Over here!

161
00:09:30,278 --> 00:09:32,822
Tsuge… He's already here…

162
00:09:36,325 --> 00:09:37,159
That idiot!

163
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:39,412
You're the bastard who killed Unno!

164
00:09:48,296 --> 00:09:49,255
Sasuke!

165
00:09:55,553 --> 00:09:57,805
Found you.

166
00:10:00,391 --> 00:10:03,352
Bind, Secure, Conceal, Ironize.

167
00:10:15,239 --> 00:10:16,657
The bullets aren't doing anything…

168
00:10:16,741 --> 00:10:18,117
Over here!

169
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:20,536
Ninja Art: Flame Release!

170
00:10:45,394 --> 00:10:46,395
Saizo!

171
00:10:58,240 --> 00:10:59,325
Yuri!

172
00:10:59,408 --> 00:11:01,118
Stay out of my way.

173
00:11:07,792 --> 00:11:09,210
Mist Concealment.

174
00:11:09,293 --> 00:11:10,252
MIST CONCEALMENT

175
00:11:11,921 --> 00:11:13,464
Now! Run!

176
00:11:30,231 --> 00:11:31,148
Mother!

177
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:35,361
I hear you leaked
Iga's secrets to outsiders.

178
00:11:36,946 --> 00:11:38,280
By order of the code,

179
00:11:38,948 --> 00:11:40,032
you must die.

180
00:11:40,116 --> 00:11:41,826
Please spare my child!

181
00:11:50,418 --> 00:11:51,502
Father!

182
00:11:53,170 --> 00:11:54,255
Saizo.

183
00:11:54,922 --> 00:11:56,132
You do it.

184
00:12:02,346 --> 00:12:03,639
Saizo…

185
00:12:24,285 --> 00:12:25,870
Letting emotions control you?

186
00:12:26,996 --> 00:12:28,622
You're no ninja.

187
00:12:44,638 --> 00:12:47,141
If you do this, you'll be…

188
00:12:49,059 --> 00:12:50,019
Yuri…

189
00:12:52,521 --> 00:12:53,397
Are you hurt?

190
00:12:54,565 --> 00:12:56,108
Nothing serious.

191
00:13:20,508 --> 00:13:22,343
-Saizo?
-You're awake.

192
00:13:23,219 --> 00:13:24,053
Are you hurt?

193
00:13:25,221 --> 00:13:26,347
Nothing serious.

194
00:13:27,556 --> 00:13:29,183
I'm sorry. This is all my fault.

195
00:13:32,937 --> 00:13:34,355
I won't let you die.

196
00:13:37,358 --> 00:13:38,192
Nothing.

197
00:13:38,734 --> 00:13:39,568
You two.

198
00:13:40,986 --> 00:13:41,946
Where are the others?

199
00:13:43,489 --> 00:13:44,615
We got separated.

200
00:13:46,367 --> 00:13:48,577
Let's head for the abandoned village
Anayama mentioned.

201
00:14:01,340 --> 00:14:03,634
Okuni! Okuni!

202
00:14:04,677 --> 00:14:07,304
Okuni! Hurry, run…

203
00:14:20,484 --> 00:14:21,485
Why…

204
00:14:22,444 --> 00:14:23,863
It's my orders.

205
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:25,489
Lord Tsuge has apparently found

206
00:14:25,573 --> 00:14:27,825
Yukimura and his men at Zao Pass.

207
00:14:27,908 --> 00:14:29,243
-Let's go.
-Yes, sir.

208
00:14:32,496 --> 00:14:36,000
Ready or not, here I come!

209
00:14:38,252 --> 00:14:40,045
You're late, all of you.

210
00:14:40,838 --> 00:14:44,258
Only Lord Hanzo
can keep up with Lord Tsuge.

211
00:14:45,551 --> 00:14:47,928
Where's Yukimura?

212
00:14:49,096 --> 00:14:50,723
Still searching.

213
00:14:55,811 --> 00:14:59,690
Ready or not, here I come!

214
00:15:00,816 --> 00:15:01,901
Don't make a sound!

215
00:15:06,864 --> 00:15:08,699
They're close…

216
00:15:10,993 --> 00:15:14,079
If they were samurai, it'd be different.
But capture even one ninja,

217
00:15:14,163 --> 00:15:16,582
and we can make him reveal
Yukimura's location.

218
00:15:17,666 --> 00:15:20,502
That's all their comradeship amounts to.

219
00:15:30,512 --> 00:15:33,641
Found you.

220
00:15:38,103 --> 00:15:39,772
Where's Yukimura?

221
00:15:39,855 --> 00:15:41,941
How should I know?

222
00:15:42,524 --> 00:15:44,276
Tell me, and you'll be rewarded.

223
00:15:44,818 --> 00:15:45,861
A reward?

224
00:15:46,654 --> 00:15:47,863
No, really, I don't know.

225
00:15:53,994 --> 00:15:54,954
You're lying.

226
00:15:55,579 --> 00:15:56,622
Die!

227
00:16:01,418 --> 00:16:03,379
I give up! I know!

228
00:16:03,462 --> 00:16:04,421
I know!

229
00:16:05,005 --> 00:16:06,256
I'll take you to Yukimura!

230
00:16:18,352 --> 00:16:21,146
I hope Sasuke's all right.

231
00:16:21,939 --> 00:16:24,316
Now's no time to worry about him.

232
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:27,027
They know we're in this area.

233
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:29,905
The enemy is everywhere.

234
00:16:29,989 --> 00:16:31,407
They're searching for us in force.

235
00:16:32,992 --> 00:16:35,494
Hattori Hanzo is probably
heading here too.

236
00:16:36,161 --> 00:16:38,455
If Hanzo and Tsuge join forces…

237
00:16:39,289 --> 00:16:40,124
it's over.

238
00:17:15,993 --> 00:17:17,828
Search below.

239
00:17:17,911 --> 00:17:18,787
Yes, sir!

240
00:17:33,635 --> 00:17:35,137
My lord, are you all right?

241
00:17:35,721 --> 00:17:37,598
Yuri, Kakei.

242
00:17:40,893 --> 00:17:42,102
Lord Yukimura.

243
00:17:43,979 --> 00:17:45,314
We must leave at once.

244
00:17:45,939 --> 00:17:46,940
Can we get away?

245
00:17:48,776 --> 00:17:52,029
I'll disguise myself as Lord Yukimura
and draw the enemy away.

246
00:17:53,322 --> 00:17:54,156
That could work.

247
00:17:55,824 --> 00:17:56,867
Lord Yukimura, please.

248
00:18:01,413 --> 00:18:03,165
Our comrades aren't all here yet.

249
00:18:04,958 --> 00:18:06,543
I won't leave anyone behind.

250
00:18:08,670 --> 00:18:10,005
Can I ask you something?

251
00:18:11,173 --> 00:18:13,717
Are all lords in this country like you?

252
00:18:14,968 --> 00:18:15,928
My lord is…

253
00:18:19,389 --> 00:18:20,516
one of a kind.

254
00:18:22,976 --> 00:18:26,063
But if we delay,
the enemy will only grow in number.

255
00:18:27,147 --> 00:18:28,482
And Hanzo too…

256
00:18:30,776 --> 00:18:32,861
Let me wait here

257
00:18:34,279 --> 00:18:35,823
for half an hour.

258
00:18:53,841 --> 00:18:56,009
Hey, how much longer?

259
00:18:57,010 --> 00:18:58,804
We're almost there. After you.

260
00:19:00,013 --> 00:19:01,765
Please.

261
00:19:40,179 --> 00:19:41,972
Isa, Seikai.

262
00:19:42,556 --> 00:19:43,807
Thank goodness you're safe.

263
00:19:44,308 --> 00:19:46,935
Now it's just Nezu and Sasuke.

264
00:19:48,478 --> 00:19:50,772
Nezu was…

265
00:19:51,481 --> 00:19:54,484
He was with the enemy.

266
00:19:54,568 --> 00:19:55,944
He's probably heading here now.

267
00:19:57,821 --> 00:19:58,780
He has betrayed us?

268
00:19:59,364 --> 00:20:01,116
Lord Yukimura, as I suggested…

269
00:20:02,117 --> 00:20:03,285
I told you.

270
00:20:03,368 --> 00:20:06,079
We're not like the Tokugawa.

271
00:20:06,163 --> 00:20:08,498
Our bonds can also be our weakness.

272
00:20:09,374 --> 00:20:10,709
Saizo is right.

273
00:20:11,335 --> 00:20:13,629
If our lord falls, it's all over.

274
00:20:14,630 --> 00:20:16,882
For us and the Toyotomi.

275
00:20:18,217 --> 00:20:19,092
Lord Yukimura.

276
00:20:21,345 --> 00:20:23,305
It's not been half an hour yet, has it?

277
00:20:26,475 --> 00:20:27,726
All right!

278
00:20:27,809 --> 00:20:29,102
In times like these…

279
00:20:30,020 --> 00:20:31,063
let's eat while we wait.

280
00:20:32,272 --> 00:20:33,273
Right?

281
00:20:33,357 --> 00:20:34,358
Come on, Saizo.

282
00:20:40,239 --> 00:20:42,449
Hey. What's taking so long?

283
00:20:42,950 --> 00:20:45,702
Sorry. Looks like I got a little lost.

284
00:20:47,579 --> 00:20:48,538
Lord Tsuge.

285
00:20:49,373 --> 00:20:51,166
I find this man suspicious.

286
00:20:51,833 --> 00:20:54,586
Did you trick me?

287
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:57,798
Of course not.

288
00:20:59,049 --> 00:21:01,093
Something's fishy.

289
00:21:01,677 --> 00:21:04,429
Damn it… I've got no choice.

290
00:21:06,056 --> 00:21:07,349
Ninja art…

291
00:21:07,432 --> 00:21:09,142
There's Lord Yukimura!

292
00:21:13,522 --> 00:21:16,024
You think you'd get away
with such a cheap trick?

293
00:21:17,943 --> 00:21:19,569
Yeah, figured as much.

294
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:24,574
Four-two, even.

295
00:21:25,242 --> 00:21:27,411
Guess my luck's run out.

296
00:21:29,955 --> 00:21:32,207
Move! Move, move!

297
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:33,375
Sasuke.

298
00:21:40,382 --> 00:21:42,801
Sasuke! What are you doing?

299
00:21:43,635 --> 00:21:44,720
I was testing it.

300
00:21:47,556 --> 00:21:49,641
This marks the 30-ken distance.

301
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:52,978
-Let's go.
-Right!

302
00:21:55,689 --> 00:21:57,357
So my dice were wrong after all…

303
00:22:06,325 --> 00:22:09,911
Half an hour has passed.

304
00:22:22,424 --> 00:22:23,842
No way…

305
00:22:29,389 --> 00:22:31,475
Found you.

306
00:22:39,107 --> 00:22:40,567
Did I sound like him?

307
00:22:40,650 --> 00:22:42,360
Sasuke! Nezu!

308
00:22:42,444 --> 00:22:44,738
Don't scare us like that!

309
00:22:44,821 --> 00:22:45,655
You…

310
00:22:45,739 --> 00:22:47,240
That's nothing to joke about!

311
00:22:47,324 --> 00:22:49,785
Nezu, didn't you defect to the enemy?

312
00:22:49,868 --> 00:22:51,912
Yeah, it was all an act.

313
00:22:52,496 --> 00:22:53,955
-What?
-Seikai.

314
00:22:54,039 --> 00:22:55,707
I need to ask you for a favor later.

315
00:23:00,337 --> 00:23:02,881
Welcome back, both of you.

316
00:23:04,716 --> 00:23:06,384
Eat up. I saved you some food.

317
00:23:08,386 --> 00:23:09,387
Much obliged.

318
00:23:13,558 --> 00:23:16,478
All right. Let's go.

319
00:23:17,354 --> 00:23:19,106
Go where?

320
00:23:19,189 --> 00:23:20,607
The river, of course.

321
00:23:20,690 --> 00:23:22,984
I'll jump across that river myself.

322
00:23:23,068 --> 00:23:25,153
I just have to tie the rope
to the other bank, right?

323
00:23:25,237 --> 00:23:27,489
There's no way you can do that.

324
00:23:29,491 --> 00:23:31,284
Saizo will act as a decoy.

325
00:23:31,368 --> 00:23:33,203
Use that chance to circle around.

326
00:23:33,286 --> 00:23:34,538
No.

327
00:23:34,621 --> 00:23:37,165
I hate being ordered around.

328
00:23:38,583 --> 00:23:41,336
Besides, wasn't this your plan?

329
00:23:41,962 --> 00:23:43,797
I thought it was a good one.

330
00:23:44,756 --> 00:23:46,550
Have a little faith in yourself.

331
00:23:47,801 --> 00:23:48,718
Don't worry.

332
00:23:49,594 --> 00:23:50,762
I can do it.

333
00:23:54,933 --> 00:23:56,434
Lord Yukimura.

334
00:24:03,984 --> 00:24:04,901
I'm…

335
00:24:07,279 --> 00:24:08,530
I'm staying here.

336
00:24:20,500 --> 00:24:21,751
Why didn't you say anything?

337
00:24:21,835 --> 00:24:23,128
Seikai!

338
00:24:26,339 --> 00:24:28,925
We have to get to Osaka quickly!

339
00:24:29,009 --> 00:24:30,010
Let's leave…

340
00:24:31,553 --> 00:24:33,305
I can't cross like this.

341
00:24:33,388 --> 00:24:35,682
Lord Yukimura, let me be the decoy, then.

342
00:24:35,765 --> 00:24:37,475
Don't worry about me.

343
00:24:38,894 --> 00:24:40,812
I'll only hold you back anyway.

344
00:24:46,818 --> 00:24:48,695
I'm counting on you
to protect Lord Yukimura.

345
00:24:52,199 --> 00:24:53,575
What do you think

346
00:24:55,577 --> 00:24:57,370
we've endured 14 years for?

347
00:25:07,047 --> 00:25:08,423
Do not worry, my lord.

348
00:25:10,383 --> 00:25:11,676
I'll make it through.

349
00:25:18,099 --> 00:25:19,976
I suppose that's our only option.

350
00:25:24,898 --> 00:25:27,484
Damn it.
Why do you always give up so easily?

351
00:25:28,735 --> 00:25:32,822
If that's what you call loyalty,
then it's bullshit.

352
00:25:34,407 --> 00:25:35,742
That's enough.

353
00:25:36,660 --> 00:25:38,703
Don't trample on Yuri's resolve.

354
00:25:43,875 --> 00:25:45,460
I'll carry her across.

355
00:25:51,549 --> 00:25:53,885
There's no way you can do that.

356
00:25:53,969 --> 00:25:54,928
I can.

357
00:25:56,346 --> 00:25:57,889
Don't give up before we've even tried.

358
00:26:00,809 --> 00:26:02,435
Sasuke's right.

359
00:26:05,188 --> 00:26:10,151
Everyone here, except Lord Yukimura,
suspected him.

360
00:26:11,152 --> 00:26:15,740
And none of us thought
Sasuke would ever come back, either.

361
00:26:16,491 --> 00:26:19,953
But look at them. They're both back.

362
00:26:22,372 --> 00:26:23,540
That's right!

363
00:26:25,166 --> 00:26:26,543
I think it's too soon

364
00:26:27,836 --> 00:26:29,004
to give up.

365
00:26:35,552 --> 00:26:36,928
Double fives. Even.

366
00:26:37,637 --> 00:26:39,097
Not a bad roll.

367
00:26:40,390 --> 00:26:42,517
My lord, what are your orders?

368
00:26:49,691 --> 00:26:50,775
We are…

369
00:26:51,776 --> 00:26:53,653
all going to Osaka.

370
00:26:55,989 --> 00:26:57,657
No one gets left behind.

371
00:27:05,749 --> 00:27:06,750
Yes, my lord.

372
00:27:30,440 --> 00:27:31,441
Lord Hanzo!

373
00:27:31,524 --> 00:27:32,817
What of Yukimura?

374
00:27:32,901 --> 00:27:34,027
My apologies!

375
00:27:34,611 --> 00:27:35,862
But rest assured.

376
00:27:35,945 --> 00:27:38,198
We're doing everything we can to find him.

377
00:27:38,281 --> 00:27:40,909
We'll bring him in shortly.

378
00:27:40,992 --> 00:27:42,494
Don't get the wrong idea.

379
00:27:43,745 --> 00:27:46,581
This is a direct order
from the Ogosho himself.

380
00:27:47,624 --> 00:27:49,376
You know what happens
if you let him escape…

381
00:27:50,835 --> 00:27:51,836
don't you?

382
00:27:54,881 --> 00:27:56,007
I'll bring him in at once.

383
00:27:58,176 --> 00:28:00,261
Sasuke, I'm counting on you.

384
00:28:00,345 --> 00:28:01,179
Leave it to me.

385
00:28:01,846 --> 00:28:03,556
Sarutobi Sasuke's on the job.

386
00:28:07,685 --> 00:28:09,020
He's been alive all this time.

387
00:28:13,024 --> 00:28:14,484
Do you remember that promise?

388
00:28:15,235 --> 00:28:18,655
When we get to Osaka,
how about we go eat konpeito together?

389
00:28:20,407 --> 00:28:21,950
Konpeito, then.

390
00:28:22,575 --> 00:28:24,828
I'll even join you for dango.

391
00:28:26,287 --> 00:28:28,331
Hold on tight.

392
00:28:47,183 --> 00:28:48,143
That far?

393
00:28:53,106 --> 00:28:54,357
This feels great!

394
00:28:54,441 --> 00:28:55,483
Watch where you're going!

395
00:29:11,207 --> 00:29:12,792
That was close.

396
00:29:14,961 --> 00:29:15,962
You okay?

397
00:29:27,390 --> 00:29:28,767
Thank goodness!

398
00:29:28,850 --> 00:29:30,477
Well done, Sasuke.

399
00:29:46,951 --> 00:29:48,620
Almost there, old man!

400
00:30:09,766 --> 00:30:12,143
You saved us, Okuni.

401
00:30:13,686 --> 00:30:14,646
Now, it's just…

402
00:30:24,948 --> 00:30:27,200
Brother, do your best.

403
00:30:30,703 --> 00:30:33,206
Hurry, Isa! The enemy's coming!

404
00:30:39,671 --> 00:30:40,839
I can't do it!

405
00:30:41,714 --> 00:30:43,174
I can't!

406
00:30:43,258 --> 00:30:46,302
Get a hold of yourself! You can do it!

407
00:30:46,886 --> 00:30:49,389
Sasuke's right! Come on!

408
00:30:52,684 --> 00:30:53,977
Isa!

409
00:30:55,103 --> 00:30:57,146
Isa! You'll be okay!

410
00:30:57,230 --> 00:30:58,857
-You'll be okay!
-Brother…

411
00:30:58,940 --> 00:31:00,358
Isa!

412
00:31:01,776 --> 00:31:03,570
Isa!

413
00:31:06,072 --> 00:31:07,031
Keep going!

414
00:31:13,371 --> 00:31:14,414
Brother!

415
00:31:33,850 --> 00:31:35,727
You're all right! Hurry up!

416
00:31:40,064 --> 00:31:41,065
Kakei. Mochizuki.

417
00:31:41,149 --> 00:31:42,150
Right!

418
00:31:43,860 --> 00:31:46,487
-Hurry up!
-Kakei, now!

419
00:31:46,571 --> 00:31:48,031
Shoot now!

420
00:31:56,205 --> 00:31:57,248
Come on, pull!

421
00:31:57,332 --> 00:31:58,583
Heave-ho!

422
00:31:59,751 --> 00:32:00,919
Heave-ho!

423
00:32:02,170 --> 00:32:03,421
Heave-ho!

424
00:32:10,720 --> 00:32:11,971
What the hell are you doing?

425
00:32:12,055 --> 00:32:13,848
We did it!

426
00:32:13,932 --> 00:32:15,642
Sorry to keep you waiting!

427
00:32:15,725 --> 00:32:17,352
I thought I was a goner.

428
00:32:20,897 --> 00:32:21,981
I told you all,

429
00:32:22,732 --> 00:32:24,108
didn't I?

430
00:32:24,192 --> 00:32:25,985
A bundle of threads can never be cut.

431
00:32:43,002 --> 00:32:45,880
Let's go. To Osaka!

432
00:32:51,636 --> 00:32:52,762
Lord Hanzo.

433
00:32:54,389 --> 00:32:55,682
So that ninja is…

434
00:32:58,810 --> 00:33:00,019
Sasuke.

435
00:33:04,607 --> 00:33:06,693
I'll make you pay!

436
00:33:16,452 --> 00:33:18,955
-Are you all right?
-I'm fine.

437
00:33:21,040 --> 00:33:23,126
What do you make of him?

438
00:33:25,044 --> 00:33:26,212
I don't know.

439
00:33:27,213 --> 00:33:28,589
He's nothing like us.

440
00:33:29,382 --> 00:33:31,592
Yeah, that's true.

441
00:33:32,552 --> 00:33:37,974
But he'll do whatever it takes
to forge a path where none exists.

442
00:33:39,684 --> 00:33:43,104
The world to come will need men like him.

443
00:33:44,397 --> 00:33:45,565
That's my feeling.

444
00:33:47,567 --> 00:33:50,028
Hey, how was my leap?

445
00:33:54,824 --> 00:33:55,908
Just a hunch, though.

446
00:34:02,832 --> 00:34:04,417
All right, everyone!

447
00:34:04,500 --> 00:34:07,295
We're almost there!

448
00:34:07,378 --> 00:34:10,089
Found you.

449
00:34:10,173 --> 00:34:13,176
Come on, Sasuke. Please stop…

450
00:34:20,683 --> 00:34:22,018
They're here!

451
00:34:22,769 --> 00:34:24,812
Lord Daisuke, stand back!

452
00:34:26,064 --> 00:34:29,067
Bind, Secure, Conceal, Ironize.

453
00:34:42,121 --> 00:34:43,206
What a pain…

454
00:34:43,706 --> 00:34:46,959
I'll kill the first one who comes at me.

455
00:34:52,632 --> 00:34:54,926
How do you like it?

456
00:34:55,009 --> 00:34:58,221
What you just took was
a powerful laxative I made.

457
00:34:59,514 --> 00:35:00,515
What?

458
00:35:00,598 --> 00:35:02,725
The main ingredient is deer droppings.

459
00:35:04,644 --> 00:35:06,479
This is what you use, right?

460
00:35:08,731 --> 00:35:11,651
So this medicine is the secret
to your strength after all.

461
00:35:20,368 --> 00:35:23,287
You said ninja don't care
about their comrades.

462
00:35:24,413 --> 00:35:25,540
Well, we do!

463
00:35:26,124 --> 00:35:28,751
We're nothing like you!

464
00:35:30,169 --> 00:35:31,295
Flame Release!

465
00:36:12,211 --> 00:36:13,421
BOMB

466
00:36:36,068 --> 00:36:37,612
You had to steal my moment.

467
00:36:37,695 --> 00:36:39,530
You took too long. That was close.

468
00:36:39,614 --> 00:36:42,158
You were struggling too.

469
00:36:45,578 --> 00:36:47,705
If those two could just get in sync…

470
00:36:47,788 --> 00:36:48,706
Yeah.

471
00:36:55,796 --> 00:36:58,341
We are the Sanada Ten Braves.

472
00:36:58,424 --> 00:37:00,760
When our ten strengths unite as one,

473
00:37:01,344 --> 00:37:04,013
no foe, however mighty, can break us.

474
00:37:06,432 --> 00:37:07,975
You underestimated our bond.

475
00:37:09,477 --> 00:37:10,811
That was your undoing.

476
00:37:12,647 --> 00:37:15,107
You'll pay for Unno's death.

477
00:37:28,371 --> 00:37:30,748
Damn it. The bastard just won't stay down.

478
00:37:31,624 --> 00:37:33,542
I can't believe he still had that in him.

479
00:37:33,626 --> 00:37:34,835
But we won!

480
00:37:34,919 --> 00:37:37,880
We actually beat Tsuge! Amazing!

481
00:37:40,549 --> 00:37:42,843
You all did well.

482
00:37:42,927 --> 00:37:43,761
Yes, my lord.

483
00:37:55,606 --> 00:37:58,859
I mean, what's with this whole
Sanada Ten Braves thing?

484
00:38:00,069 --> 00:38:01,320
Don't be embarrassed.

485
00:38:01,904 --> 00:38:02,863
I'm not embarrassed.

486
00:38:07,994 --> 00:38:10,997
OSAKA CASTLE

487
00:38:14,166 --> 00:38:15,626
Open the gates!

488
00:38:17,003 --> 00:38:22,133
Lord Sanada Yukimura has arrived!

489
00:38:24,677 --> 00:38:26,387
A welcoming feast, perhaps?

490
00:38:26,470 --> 00:38:28,139
A feast?

491
00:38:28,222 --> 00:38:29,390
Of course!

492
00:38:30,057 --> 00:38:33,019
The hero who's come to save them
in their hour of need is here!

493
00:38:34,103 --> 00:38:35,062
A feast, huh?

494
00:38:40,693 --> 00:38:41,736
Who are these men?

495
00:38:42,862 --> 00:38:43,738
We are…

496
00:38:45,114 --> 00:38:46,782
the peerless ninja squad,

497
00:38:47,450 --> 00:38:49,201
-the Sanada Ten Braves--
-Please leave.

498
00:38:50,161 --> 00:38:51,996
Ninja aren't allowed in the castle.

499
00:38:52,705 --> 00:38:53,539
What?

500
00:38:55,207 --> 00:38:57,084
You let Yukimura escape?

501
00:38:57,168 --> 00:38:59,253
My apologies, my lord.

502
00:39:00,713 --> 00:39:01,922
Atone for it with your life!

503
00:39:04,759 --> 00:39:05,593
Yes, my lord.

504
00:39:05,676 --> 00:39:06,761
Hold on.

505
00:39:07,720 --> 00:39:10,514
It's not all bad.

506
00:39:12,141 --> 00:39:16,270
Yukimura entering Osaka Castle
gives us the perfect pretext for war.

507
00:39:17,063 --> 00:39:19,940
Now we have grounds
to attack the Toyotomi.

508
00:39:20,649 --> 00:39:23,486
The people of the realm will accept it.

509
00:39:24,737 --> 00:39:26,864
Thank you, my lord!
Next time, I'll get him!

510
00:39:27,656 --> 00:39:28,699
Still,

511
00:39:29,283 --> 00:39:32,203
you couldn't kill a single one
of Sanada's ninja?

512
00:39:33,537 --> 00:39:36,207
Perhaps it's time to retrain your men.

513
00:39:37,124 --> 00:39:38,417
Quite right.

514
00:39:45,800 --> 00:39:46,717
Here you are.

515
00:39:53,516 --> 00:39:54,475
Lord Hanzo…

516
00:39:55,518 --> 00:39:56,394
You fool.

517
00:40:01,941 --> 00:40:03,692
I, Sanada Yukimura,

518
00:40:04,819 --> 00:40:07,738
have arrived, though belatedly.

519
00:40:08,823 --> 00:40:10,533
You've come at last.

520
00:40:10,616 --> 00:40:11,450
ONO HARUNAGA

521
00:40:11,534 --> 00:40:14,912
Your journey from Kudoyama
must have been arduous.

522
00:40:16,247 --> 00:40:18,749
After coming all this way,

523
00:40:18,833 --> 00:40:21,001
why do we have to hide
in a place like this?

524
00:40:22,503 --> 00:40:23,754
I'm starving.

525
00:40:25,047 --> 00:40:27,800
So much for a feast.
Got my hopes up for nothing.

526
00:40:28,676 --> 00:40:30,886
Even as Lord Yukimura's retainers,

527
00:40:30,970 --> 00:40:33,347
we're still just ninja to them.

528
00:40:34,932 --> 00:40:37,560
Are ninja really so hated?

529
00:40:38,394 --> 00:40:41,772
Shady outsiders
who use underhanded tactics.

530
00:40:42,523 --> 00:40:45,443
That's how they see us,
especially the samurai.

531
00:40:47,611 --> 00:40:48,988
I see.

532
00:40:49,071 --> 00:40:51,866
Lord Daisuke, why are you here too?

533
00:40:53,325 --> 00:40:55,411
There's nothing
for me to do in the castle.

534
00:41:03,210 --> 00:41:04,587
I want to be as strong…

535
00:41:07,006 --> 00:41:08,090
as a ninja!

536
00:41:12,136 --> 00:41:13,012
So…

537
00:41:14,680 --> 00:41:17,141
All right. Come with me.

538
00:41:17,850 --> 00:41:19,685
First, we gather intelligence.

539
00:41:19,768 --> 00:41:21,520
Let's see how the war council is going.

540
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:23,481
Yes!

541
00:41:23,564 --> 00:41:26,108
I'd like to see Lady Yodo too. Come on.

542
00:41:26,859 --> 00:41:27,902
Understood!

543
00:41:28,903 --> 00:41:29,904
Still…

544
00:41:30,654 --> 00:41:33,574
you've brought a mere ten men with you.

545
00:41:34,241 --> 00:41:36,744
And most of them are ninja.

546
00:41:37,870 --> 00:41:43,584
So the Sanada clan owed its strength
to your father, Lord Masayuki.

547
00:41:44,168 --> 00:41:47,046
There's nothing less trustworthy
than a ninja.

548
00:41:47,129 --> 00:41:48,380
ODA URAKUSAI

549
00:41:48,464 --> 00:41:52,176
I'd sooner deal with the ronin.

550
00:41:52,259 --> 00:41:53,427
GOTO MATABE

551
00:41:59,725 --> 00:42:01,101
Acting all high and mighty.

552
00:42:01,810 --> 00:42:02,937
Who do they think they are?

553
00:42:04,271 --> 00:42:05,648
Without further ado,

554
00:42:06,315 --> 00:42:09,902
what plan do you propose?

555
00:42:10,653 --> 00:42:11,737
A plan?

556
00:42:11,820 --> 00:42:13,322
They don't have one.

557
00:42:14,031 --> 00:42:15,199
I'm Goto Matabe.

558
00:42:15,908 --> 00:42:18,911
These fools don't know
the first thing about war.

559
00:42:18,994 --> 00:42:20,204
How dare you!

560
00:42:20,913 --> 00:42:23,207
A mere ronin should know his place.

561
00:42:24,250 --> 00:42:27,586
Then allow me to lay out my plan.

562
00:42:32,424 --> 00:42:34,927
KAMEYAMA

563
00:42:35,010 --> 00:42:37,888
Ieyasu will soon enter Nijo Castle

564
00:42:37,972 --> 00:42:39,974
to launch an attack on Osaka.

565
00:42:41,809 --> 00:42:46,272
We'll strike Fushimi
before its forces are ready.

566
00:42:47,106 --> 00:42:48,023
KYOTO
FUSHIMI

567
00:42:48,107 --> 00:42:49,483
Using that as our foothold,

568
00:42:50,651 --> 00:42:55,781
we'll storm Nijo Castle,
and before Hidetada's forces arrive…

569
00:42:57,324 --> 00:42:59,827
we'll take Ieyasu's head.

570
00:43:02,580 --> 00:43:04,331
With Ieyasu dead,

571
00:43:04,415 --> 00:43:08,252
the warlords loyal to the Tokugawa
will have no reason to fight.

572
00:43:09,336 --> 00:43:12,339
They will readily switch sides
and join us.

573
00:43:12,423 --> 00:43:13,716
KYOTO
OSAKA NARA

574
00:43:13,799 --> 00:43:15,551
We'll bring them over to our side

575
00:43:16,343 --> 00:43:19,763
and use their troops
to strike Hidetada from behind.

576
00:43:21,432 --> 00:43:23,934
That will win us the war.

577
00:43:25,561 --> 00:43:27,438
Once Hidetada's forces arrive,

578
00:43:28,397 --> 00:43:30,441
the enemy will number over 100,000.

579
00:43:31,650 --> 00:43:33,527
We mustn't let this chance slip away.

580
00:43:43,704 --> 00:43:46,332
That's incredible. Just as I'd expect.

581
00:43:47,708 --> 00:43:48,542
Right.

582
00:43:48,626 --> 00:43:49,835
It's settled, then.

583
00:43:51,962 --> 00:43:53,297
Lady Yodo.

584
00:43:59,928 --> 00:44:00,929
Nobushige.

585
00:44:02,431 --> 00:44:03,390
Lady Yodo.

586
00:44:04,266 --> 00:44:06,352
I go by Yukimura now.

587
00:44:07,645 --> 00:44:10,648
I apologize for my late arrival.

588
00:44:13,651 --> 00:44:14,985
I, Sanada Yukimura,

589
00:44:16,403 --> 00:44:17,946
have arrived.

590
00:44:24,495 --> 00:44:26,622
So that's Lady Yodo.

591
00:44:31,960 --> 00:44:33,379
Nobushige,

592
00:44:33,462 --> 00:44:36,465
why didn't you come to me at once?

593
00:44:37,383 --> 00:44:39,134
The Tokugawa forces are closing in.

594
00:44:39,843 --> 00:44:42,429
Every moment counts,
so we must hold the war council first.

595
00:44:42,513 --> 00:44:45,724
That can wait.

596
00:44:45,808 --> 00:44:47,351
Oh my…

597
00:44:47,434 --> 00:44:49,436
"That can wait"?

598
00:44:50,229 --> 00:44:51,105
But…

599
00:44:52,147 --> 00:44:54,525
If the enemy attacks,
we'll just hold out here.

600
00:44:55,567 --> 00:44:58,695
This is a magnificent castle
built by the Taiko himself.

601
00:44:59,696 --> 00:45:01,532
It can never fall.

602
00:45:02,699 --> 00:45:04,660
Isn't that right?

603
00:45:05,244 --> 00:45:06,328
Yes.

604
00:45:07,913 --> 00:45:11,208
Osaka Castle is certainly well-fortified.

605
00:45:11,750 --> 00:45:12,626
But…

606
00:45:13,252 --> 00:45:17,047
holding out under siege only works
when we can count on reinforcements.

607
00:45:18,215 --> 00:45:20,926
Even if we hold out for a while,
sooner or later…

608
00:45:21,009 --> 00:45:22,636
A sortie is out of the question!

609
00:45:23,887 --> 00:45:27,891
What if anything happened to Hideyori?

610
00:45:29,685 --> 00:45:32,229
Holding out here is our only option.

611
00:45:33,647 --> 00:45:34,606
This council is over.

612
00:45:38,152 --> 00:45:39,278
Lord Hideyori!

613
00:45:40,195 --> 00:45:43,198
What do you think, Lord Hideyori?

614
00:46:11,435 --> 00:46:12,478
As my mother…

615
00:46:13,687 --> 00:46:14,938
commands.

616
00:46:15,022 --> 00:46:16,064
TOYOTOMI HIDEYORI

617
00:46:16,815 --> 00:46:17,858
What is going on?

618
00:46:28,911 --> 00:46:31,121
Subtitle translation by: Sayo Takada

619
00:46:31,205 --> 00:46:33,165
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION
